    "description": "In this video, Chef John makes Bavarian pretzels using a baking soda bath. This recipe dates back to the 1800’s where it used a lye bath to coat the dough, which he substitutes with baking soda. After kneading the dough into a smooth ball, flatten it out and divide it into 8 portions. Shape them into pretzel shapes and soak each one in the baking soda bath. Finally, bake the pretzels in the oven for around 12 minutes. This crunchy and salty snack is a baked delight!",
